# Testing

## Context

Existing tests (`app/src/lib/text.test.ts`, `app/src/reducer.test.ts`,
`app/src/store.test.ts`) are colocated vitest files and are the baseline
"green" state (`cd app && npm test`).

## Rule

- Tests live **colocated** next to the code they cover, named `*.test.ts`
  (e.g. a new `app/src/foo.ts` gets `app/src/foo.test.ts`).
- Use **vitest** (`describe`/`it`/`expect`), matching the style already in
  `app/src/reducer.test.ts`.
- Structure each test **Arrange-Act-Assert**: build input state/action, act
  (dispatch or call the function), assert on the result.
- Any new `Action` variant gets at least one reducer test (state transition)
  and, if it has an action creator, a test for the creator's output shape.
- Never delete or weaken an existing assertion to make a change pass —
  fix the implementation instead.

## How to verify

1. `cd app && npm test` exits 0.
2. Every new/changed source file under `app/src` has a corresponding
   `*.test.ts` that was added or updated in the same change.
3. Test file names and `describe` blocks match the vitest style already used
   in the repo (no new test runner/framework introduced).
